  "scientific_conclusion": [
    "The supervised two-stage intervention reduces V31 Q4 from 12.43, 6.35, and 2.21 to 1.02, 1.41, and 0.54 in TNG100, SIMBA, and Swift. TNG100 and Swift also pass both frozen Q3 checks; SIMBA misses q99.999 by only 0.012 dex.",
    "This tail repair is not a usable density-field realization. The global residual amplitude scale is only 0.045 to 0.161 on average and sits at a boundary for 25.0 to 37.5 percent of samples, collapsing residual RMS, ensemble coverage, rank calibration, high-k power, and peak/void statistics.",
    "The full and backbone-only risk arms have nearly identical field failures, and the rolled-risk arm retains the same qualitative failure. The dominant failure is therefore global scaling of the stochastic body, not block seams or absence of a transferable structure-risk signal.",
    "The next frozen branch must keep the V41 object-amplitude predictor but replace global residual scaling by a train-only native within-block extreme-location model and a tail-only continuous calibration. The non-extreme residual body must remain byte-identical to the unscaled V31 conditional inverse apart from exact DC projection."
  ],
